            <ArticleTitle>Clinical utility of serum folate measurement in tertiary care patients: Argument for revising reference range for serum folate from 3.0 ng/mL to 13.0 ng/mL.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.plabm.2015.03.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Assess the need for folate testing, frequency of corrective action, and determine reference level for serum folate.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Serum folate levels in 5313 samples from 4448 patients, and clinical data were reviewed for patient characteristics and for (a) evidence of corrective action in patients with serum folate values &lt;5.5 ng/mL, and (b) differences in patients with serum folate levels &lt;5.5 ng/mL and patients with levels &gt;25.7 ng/mL.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The prevalence of serum folate levels, in patients, &lt;3.0, &lt;4.0, &lt;5.5, &lt;7.0 and &lt;13.0 ng/mL was 0.58%, 1.55%, 4.9%, 9.98% and 43.21% respectively. Patients with serum folate levels &lt;5.5 ng/mL had lower serum albumin and hemoglobin. In 64% of patients with serum folate &gt;25.7 ng/mL the sample was collected after supplementation with folic acid. Of the 128 patients with serum folate &lt;5.5 ng/mL documentation of supplementation was present in only 38.9%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Serum folate levels are below the current &quot;normal&quot; level of 3.0 ng/mL in a larger proportion of tertiary care patients than that reported for ambulatory patients. In patients with folate deficiency, corrective action is lacking in &gt;60% of the patients. Since serum folate levels ≥13.0 ng/mL are needed for optimal prevention of neural tube defects in the embryo/fetus, we propose that normal serum folate level should be designated to be ≥13.0 ng/mL.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
